# gR DEV AGENT

Thin adapter — `.gr-agent/` is the single source of truth for workflow and project knowledge
(`CONTRIBUTING.md` "The one rule"). Full rules: `.gr-agent/rules/`. Architecture seams and safety
invariants: `CONTRIBUTING.md` at the repo root — read it before non-trivial work.

A vendor-neutral, parallel multi-agent engineering workflow orchestrator, published as an npm CLI.
TypeScript, Node >= 20, ESM. `src/` (platform/orchestrator/workers/llm/integrations/ui/cli),
`adapters/` (per-tool scaffold templates), `test/` (vitest).

Workflow rules:
1. Feature specs live in `.gr-agent/specs/` (template: `.gr-agent/specs/_template.md`). The spec's
   contract is the source of truth — code against it; contract changes go to the spec first.
2. New code goes in the seam it belongs to (CONTRIBUTING.md's seam table) — never bypass the
   registry/interface for that seam.
3. `integrations.manifest.json` is the ONLY place installer/login/worker-argv strings live —
   never construct these inline, and only mark an entry `"verified": true` after checking it
   against the vendor's current official docs.
4. Never weaken a safety invariant (workspace boundary, destructive-command approval, secret
   redaction, installer/login consent, write-conflict protection) to simplify a change.
5. Never: force push, direct commits on `main` for anything non-trivial, editing
   `node_modules`/`dist`, committing secrets or `package-lock.json` by hand.

Verification: `npm run build && npm test && npm run lint && npm run typecheck` — all four green.
